# Docker Compose PROJECT variables for compose.yaml. Not application secrets.
# Copy to `.env` next to compose.yaml (only if no `.env` exists yet) and set
# your real public domain. Compose reads `.env` automatically in every shell,
# so a later `docker compose up -d` keeps the same proxy domain.
# Only non-secret Compose variables belong here: STYLE_DOMAIN (required) and
# the optional STYLE_BODY_READ_TIMEOUT_MS below. That one value sets the app's
# upload-body deadline AND, plus 2 seconds, the proxy's cap, so they cannot
# drift. Whole milliseconds, 1000 to 120000, no leading zero, default 20000.
# Do NOT also put it in .env.production (the app refuses to start if you do, so nothing else starts).
# Uncomment only to change it; see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md "Proxy transport behaviour".
# STYLE_BODY_READ_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
# AUTH_SECRET, SMTP_URL and the other secrets belong in the untracked
# `.env.production`, never in this file.
# The value below is an illustrative placeholder, not a real deployment.
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
STYLE_DOMAIN=your-real-domain.example
